// v3283 -- SIX ROUNDS: EXPERIMENT DESIGN, A ZERO-TOLERANCE KERNEL, TWO NEW DEVICES, A SECOND IDENTITY, AND A NEW
//          KIND OF KEY.
//
// Prior art was checked before every round, and the check paid: symbolic law discovery (discovery-lab), the
// Feigenbaum delta and the exact ln 2 Lyapunov exponent (logistic), and Mercury's 43 arcsec/century (probe-lab)
// were ALREADY BUILT and were struck from the menu rather than duplicated. One fact, one implementation.
//
// A -- THE BRAIN ALLOCATES THE MEASUREMENT BUDGET (physics/statmech/binderBudget.js, binder-budget.html)
//   The second proposer-adjudicator handshake, one level above the HMC tuner: the tuner chose a sampler's knobs,
//   this chooses WHICH EXPERIMENT TO RUN NEXT. Strategies see the data so far and propose the next temperature;
//   they never grade themselves. At a 9-measurement budget, bisection brackets the Binder crossing to 0.0035 and
//   lands 0.0038 from Onsager; even coverage manages 0.0562 (16x wider). The DEGENERATE POLICY IS NAMED AND
//   MEASURED: easyStrategy prefers smooth low-variance data far from the transition -- exactly what a
//   "confident measurements" reward endorses -- and its bracket is 0.2180, 62x worse. Pretty data about nothing.
//   THE FALSIFIER CAUGHT THE BUILD ITSELF: the first bracketOf scanned for a positive->negative sign change,
//   which is backwards (d = U4(8) - U4(16) is NEGATIVE below Tc), so it bracketed noise flips in the ordered
//   phase and reported a crossing at 2.19. Onsager said no. The comment on the fixed function keeps the story.
//
// B -- ISING FLEET KERNEL, THE FIRST GRADED AT ZERO TOLERANCE (tools/roundhouse/isingGpu.mjs, ising-bench.html)
//   The missing fleet capability was deterministic RNG ON the GPU. Philox4x32-10 is counter-based -- no state,
//   no sequence to coordinate between threads -- and it matches BOTH Random123 known-answer vectors bit-for-bit,
//   so the kernel carries the PUBLISHED function, not one like it. The Metropolis factor never enters the
//   kernel: dE takes one of five values, so exp(-dE/T) is quantized ONCE on the CPU in f64 to u32 thresholds
//   (worst quantization 1.16e-10) and the kernel accepts iff philoxWord < threshold. Integer arithmetic end to
//   end means there is NO FLOATING-POINT FLOOR TO ARGUE ABOUT: a device must match the CPU mirror SPIN FOR SPIN.
//   Faithful run: 0/1024 differ. One bit wrong in a Philox constant: 662/1024 scrambled. And the mirror
//   reproduces Yang's exact magnetisation (0.9796 vs 0.9796 at T=1.6) -- the RNG is good enough to DO PHYSICS,
//   which no test of the stream alone can certify. Checkerboard parity dispatches keep the races out.
//   The WGSL mulhilo carries an explicit carry chain, because u32 addition wraps and the 16-bit-limb product
//   overflows without it. New fleet KIND: swek-ising-bench.
//
// C -- KURAMOTO (physics/sync/kuramoto.js, kuramoto.html) -- a new AREA for the lab: synchronization.
//   The answer key is a whole CURVE, not a point: for Lorentzian frequencies, K_c = 2*gamma and
//   r(K) = sqrt(1 - Kc/K) (Ott-Antonsen), neither number anywhere in the update rule, which knows only "nudge
//   toward the crowd's average". Measured branch matches at K = 1.5, 2.0, 2.5 to 0.0066 worst; below threshold r
//   sits on the 1/sqrt(N) floor (0.0193 at N=4096). The sabotage is the plausible mean-field slip K*r^2 instead
//   of K*r: every oscillator stays locally sensible and the crowd CANNOT BOOTSTRAP from noise -- r = 0.0149
//   where the true rule gives 0.5774.
//
// D -- BOND PERCOLATION (physics/percolation/percolation.js, percolation.html)
//   The cheapest deep device in the lab, and its key is exact AT FINITE SIZE, which almost no emergent-threshold
//   claim is: by Kesten's self-duality, the horizontal crossing probability of an L x (L+1) rectangle at p = 1/2
//   is EXACTLY 1/2 for EVERY L. Measured 0.5010 (L=24) and 0.4980 (L=48) over 3000 realizations, with the
//   binomial band as the entire tolerance -- no finite-size allowance to hide in. Second key, the universal
//   exponent: doubling L shrinks the 25%-to-75% transition width by 2^(-3/4) = 0.5946 (nu = 4/3); measured
//   0.6080, obtained by nothing but counting clusters at two sizes. HONEST NOTE: the sabotage (dropping one
//   column's rightward bonds) fails LOUDLY -- it cuts the lattice and crossing probability goes to 0.0000 --
//   so it proves the key is connected to the lattice, not that the key catches subtle bias.
//
// E -- CROOKS (physics/langevin/langevin.js, gate section 7) -- the theorem Jarzynski is the average of.
//   Run the trap protocol BACKWARD as well and the two work distributions are locked together pointwise:
//   P_F(W)/P_R(-W) = exp((W - dF)/kT). Measured: the histograms cross at 0.7260 vs dF = 0.6931, and the
//   log-ratio is a line of slope 1.0309 vs 1/kT = 1.0 giving dF = 0.6905 over 37 bins. Jarzynski graded one
//   number per ensemble; Crooks grades the WHOLE DISTRIBUTION. The quiet work-ledger bug (missing the 1/2)
//   now fails a SECOND independent identity: crossing 1.4385, slope 0.5128.
//
// F -- THE CONSISTENCY BOARD (physics/consistency.mjs, consistency.html) -- A NEW KIND OF KEY.
//   Every gate before this held a measurement against algebra or against a sabotaged twin. This board holds
//   measurements against EACH OTHER: one constant, two routes independent in MECHANISM, agreement gated. That
//   is how metrology certifies numbers nobody has a closed form for. Three pairs at launch:
//     Ising T_c  -- Binder cumulant crossing 2.2379 vs Fisher amplitude-ratio chi(24)/chi(12) = 2^(7/4)
//                   crossing 2.2209 (different moments, different finite-size logic)
//     trap dF    -- Jarzynski forward average 0.6950 vs Crooks log-ratio fit 0.6871
//     LBM nu     -- configured (tau-1/2)/3 = 0.1000 vs shear-wave decay rate 0.1001 (input vs BEHAVIOUR)
//   ADMISSION RULE, written into the file: independent in mechanism, not merely in code path. Two seeds of one
//   estimator will never qualify. THE BOARD EARNED ITS STRIPES ON ITS OWN CODE: route B was first a chi-PEAK
//   1/L extrapolation; the peak is broad, its located position swung ~0.2 across seeds, and 2*p(2L) - p(L)
//   doubles that noise. The board flagged its own route as inconsistent and it was replaced with the
//   well-conditioned ratio crossing (seed spread 0.023). The sabotage is the failure shape no single-instrument
//   gate can see: a route using gamma/nu = 2 instead of the exact 7/4 stays smooth and internally consistent
//   and finds no crossing at all.
//
// REGISTRY: five new instruments (binder-budget, ising-kernel, kuramoto, percolation, consistency), 29 -> 34,
// and the jarzynski entry's key now names Crooks. Knowledge index 634 -> 639 gates.
//
