// v3285 ADDENDUM -- THE CONSISTENCY BOARD GOES FLEET-WIDE (physics/consistencyFleet.mjs, consistency-fleet.html)
//
// A peer runs ONE SIDE of a pair and submits the number; the hub assembles pairs from whatever has arrived. An
// expensive route stops being something one machine grinds through serially, and a route can be measured on
// hardware that never runs the other side at all.
//
// *** THE MISTAKE THIS ROUND EXISTS TO REFUSE. *** The moment the board is fleet-wide, the tempting move is to
// run THE SAME ROUTE on two machines, watch the numbers agree, and record a pair. They WILL agree -- the code is
// seeded and deterministic, so they had better -- and the agreement carries NO INFORMATION about the physics.
// That is one mechanism run twice: a REPRODUCIBILITY check, which the zero-tolerance kernels already do far
// better, wearing the costume of a consistency pair. A board that accepted it would certify empty agreements,
// which is worse than having no board, because it looks like evidence.
//
// So the admission rule stopped being prose and became data: every route in consistency.mjs now carries a
// machine-readable `mechanism` id, and admissible() refuses two routes that share one -- naming hosts explicitly
// as NO SUBSTITUTE for mechanism. Different hosts are recorded as a BONUS dimension of independence (a genuine
// pair measured on two toolchains is stronger than the same pair on one) and never as a replacement for it.
// Same-mechanism duplicates are surfaced AS reproducibility rather than dropped: the work was real, the claim is
// different.
//
// AND THE HUB RE-GRADES, which is the same rule the phone, the boot sidecar and the proposer registry all live
// under. Measured: a report carrying {agree:true} is REJECTED at fold time rather than believed; a peer that
// relabels its own mechanism to forge independence gets nowhere, because the mechanism is looked up LOCALLY from
// the routeId; one side reporting is INCOMPLETE and never AGREE; an empty fleet claims no pairs and says that no
// report is not the same as no disagreement. Two genuinely-run routes assemble end to end (LBM viscosity,
// 0.10000 configured vs 0.10005 shear-decay).
//
