// v3337 -- PERCEPTUAL RENDER COMPARISON. An idea lifted from img2threejs (Apache 2.0); no code copied, and its
//          thresholds deliberately left behind.
//
// physics/backendVisualDiff.mjs counts pixels differing by more than a threshold. That is the wrong question in
// TWO DIRECTIONS AT ONCE: it FAILS ON A ONE-PIXEL SHIFT -- measured, 1.5% of pixels change while SSIM stays
// 0.9581 and pHash moves 4 bits of 63 -- and it PASSES a structurally wrong render that happens to land the same
// colours in the same places, since the rasteriser's shade is a function of body index.
//
// render/perceptual.mjs adds pHash, SSIM and Sobel edge overlap; render/silhouette.mjs adds silhouette IoU and
// scale delta. EVERY METRIC HAS AN EXACT SELF-KEY, which is the price of admission here: SSIM against itself is
// exactly 1, pHash exactly 0 bits, edge overlap exactly 1, IoU exactly 1 with scale delta exactly 0. Edge overlap
// is scale-free by construction, so the same shape rendered brighter scores exactly 1 -- a lighting change that
// a pixel diff fails outright.
//
// THE HARD GATES ARE NOT AVERAGED, WHICH IS THE WHOLE IDEA WORTH TAKING. A soft score of 0.960 across tone,
// edges, structure and symmetry does NOT rescue a failed silhouette gate. Both numbers are reported side by side:
// hiding the soft score would make the rejection unarguable, and hiding the veto would make the average a lie.
// A hard gate supplied with NO LIMIT throws rather than defaulting.
//
// *** AND THEIR NUMBERS WERE NOT IMPORTED. *** img2threejs uses IoU < 0.85 and scale delta > 0.08, tuned against
// photographs of knives. Shipping those here would ship a tolerance nobody in this tree ever measured -- the
// defect this session already found in the promptCost multiplier, the "MEASURED" gate headers and the airy
// control. MEASURED ON THIS TREE'S OWN RASTERISER, THE FLOOR IS EXACT: Jolt renders bit-identically, so IoU is 1,
// scale delta 0 and pHash 0 bits over every sampled frame. The determinism gate therefore needs NO TOLERANCE AT
// ALL, which is a stronger statement than 0.85 and could only be reached by measuring rather than borrowing.
// The CROSS-BACKEND threshold is UNMEASURED and deliberately absent: box3d's WASM is built per rig and reports
// "call init() first" here, so the box3d-vs-Jolt limit is left unshipped rather than guessed. Running this gate
// on a rig with box3d prints the floor to earn one from.
//
// AND THE GATE CAUGHT A REAL FRAGILITY IN ITS OWN FIRST RUN. mask() calls anything brighter than 8 "covered",
// which is exactly right for a rasteriser drawing onto a zero-filled buffer and exactly wrong for anything else.
// The first fixtures used a background of 20, so EVERY PIXEL read as occupied and IoU returned 1.0000 for two
// boxes that do not overlap at all -- three checks passing on a saturated mask. The assumption is now documented
// and PINNED as its own check, and the threshold was deliberately NOT made adaptive: an adaptive one would
// segment something on any input, and this should be obviously wrong when misused rather than quietly plausible.
//
// Registry 52 -> 53 instruments. Knowledge index -> 693 gates.
