// v3338 -- HOW THE CROSS-BACKEND FLOOR GETS MEASURED ON A RIG, AND THE PASS THAT WAS WAITING TO HAPPEN THERE.
//
// v3337 shipped the perceptual metrics with the cross-backend threshold deliberately absent, because box3d's
// WASM is built per rig and cannot load here. The obvious next question is how that floor ever comes to exist.
// IT TURNS OUT THE MACHINERY ALREADY DID: physics/backend-qa-check.mjs has carried captureMetrics -> toBaseline
// -> gateAgainstBaseline with an --update flag since long before this, and tools/render-qa/backend-baseline.json
// has sat there since 2026-07-13 with "pairs": {} -- EMPTY, because box3d has never loaded wherever --update was
// last run. The blocker was never the mechanism. It is one WASM build.
//
// *** BUT THE FIRST RUN ON THAT RIG WOULD HAVE GONE GREEN WHILE MEASURING NOTHING. *** gateAgainstBaseline
// reported ok:true for a pair with no recorded envelope -- "record with --update" as a note attached to a PASS.
// So on the day box3d finally loads, the gate would have said GREEN, the pair would have been measured and
// discarded, and nobody would have been told. A control that cannot fail, arriving exactly at the moment the
// awaited measurement becomes possible. It is now UNMEASURED: ok:false, loud, and it prints the command.
//
// TWO CHANGES SO ONE RIG RUN IS ENOUGH:
//   (1) captureMetrics now records the PERCEPTUAL floor in the same pass -- silhouette IoU, scale delta, SSIM,
//       edge overlap and pHash bits, worst-case over the sampled frames. The frames are already in hand, so an
//       --update run captures everything at once instead of leaving the perceptual thresholds for another round.
//   (2) toBaseline envelopes them BOUNDED BOTH WAYS, for the reason the drift envelope already was: a floor with
//       only a ceiling would let two different solvers become suspiciously identical without anyone noticing,
//       and two different solvers agreeing perfectly is a finding rather than a success.
//
// BOTH PATHS ARE PROVEN HERE WITHOUT box3d, by running Jolt as two named backends so the PAIR path is exercised:
// with no envelope the gate FAILS as UNMEASURED and names the command; with the envelope recorded it gates all
// five perceptual metrics, nine checks in total. The branch is tested rather than merely written.
//
// THE PROCEDURE, therefore, is one command on a rig where box3d builds:
//     node physics/backend-qa-check.mjs --update
// and the numbers it prints become the floor. Until then the baseline says so in its own _note rather than
// looking like a recorded result that happens to be empty.
