// v3339 -- FOUR USES OF THE PERCEPTUAL WORK, AND THE STATE THAT KEEPS "RENDERED" FROM READING AS "VERIFIED".
//
// A -- *** THE FIVE PAGES THAT OWE A MEASUREMENT ARE THE FIVE NOTHING TRACKS. *** server.html already gets the
//   hard part right: its per-page list carries NEVER RUN as a state deliberately distinct from PASS, with the
//   comment "a page nobody has tested and a page that passed look the same in any list that only has two states,
//   and they are not the same claim". That list is driven by render-qa/manifest.json, which tracks 54 pages --
//   and hmc-bench, ising-bench, magmap-bench, consistency-fleet and floor-atlas are in NONE of them. They appear
//   only as links in a pageSections drawer, which records WHERE a page lives, not whether it has ever said
//   anything. Findable, and unaccountable: the machinery that would stop them being ignored points elsewhere.
//
//   AND THE OBVIOUS FIX IS A TRAP. Adding them to the manifest would show "never run", then "pass" after a rig
//   run -- but render-QA proves the page RENDERED, while these pages exist to SUBMIT A REPORT TO THE FLEET. A
//   green pass meaning "it drew something" while reading as "the kernel is verified" is worse than the current
//   silence, because it looks like an answer. tools/render-qa/deviceOwed.mjs therefore carries THREE states:
//   RENDERED / VERDICT-OWED / VERDICT-IN, and the middle one cannot be reached by rendering harder. Each page
//   names the submission kind that settles it, so "has this been done" is answered by looking rather than
//   remembering. Measured now: four owe a verdict, floor-atlas is listed as a READER owing nothing rather than
//   omitted, and received kinds is NONE.
//
// B -- PERCEPTUAL SIGNALS BESIDE pixelmatch ON ALL 54 RENDER-QA PAGES. amplifiedDiff.mjs exists because
//   "112,796 pixels, 442 differ, each by 0.3%" is unreadable -- it was built so a person could SEE a sub-percent
//   difference, which treats the symptom. Browser screenshots differ constantly for reasons that are not
//   regressions: antialiasing, font hinting, driver revision, compositor timing. SSIM, pHash and silhouette IoU
//   are the standard answer, and a one-pixel shift moves SSIM by 0.04 and pHash by 4 bits of 63 while the pixel
//   count calls it 1.5% changed.
//   THEY ARE RECORDED AND NOT GATING. The headless floor is exactly zero because Jolt is deterministic; a browser
//   is not, and no browser-screenshot floor has been measured. Gating on an unmeasured number is the failure this
//   entire line of work exists to avoid, so they run, land in the record, and a later round earns thresholds from
//   what they report.
//
// C -- AN IMAGE-BASED CONSISTENCY PAIR, DECLARED INCOMPLETE. Every pair on the board compares two SCALARS; this
//   would compare two PICTURES. The comparison is built and works, and the pair is NOT assembled, because only
//   one renderer here draws that scene. A pair made from one mechanism twice is reproducibility wearing the
//   costume of corroboration, and the admission rule does not bend for a pair that would be convenient.
//   compareRenders with no limits returns UNGATED and concludes nothing: an ensemble without a veto always has an
//   answer, which is the failure the hard/soft split prevents.
//
// D -- "NO BASELINE" STOPS MEANING "NOTHING CAN BE SAID". A page with no stored PNG now records its structural
//   fingerprint, so two runs that disagree are visibly non-deterministic BEFORE anyone freezes a baseline from
//   one of them -- and writing a baseline is the one operation in that harness that cannot be undone by running
//   it again.
//
// TWO IMAGE SHAPES, ONE NORMALISER: backendVisualDiff produces {data, w, h} and render-qa produces
// {data, width, height}. Converting at each call site is where a w/width slip eventually passes the wrong
// dimension and silently reinterprets the buffer as a different picture. dims() does it once, and the gate proves
// the same buffer under either spelling compares as exactly identical.
//
// AND A CLAIM OF MINE WAS WRONG AGAIN, CORRECTED BY THE MEASUREMENT: I asserted that a displaced render is
// "REJECTED despite strong soft agreement". It is rejected, and the soft signals COLLAPSE TOO (0.201), so nothing
// is being overridden and the check would have passed for a reason other than the one it named. The genuine
// override -- a 0.960 soft average vetoed by a failed hard gate -- is exercised in perceptual-selfcheck, where
// the soft values are supplied directly. Registry 53 -> 54. Knowledge index -> 694 gates.
