// D -- *** AND MY OWN GATE PASSED ON AN EMPTY FIT, INSIDE THE ROUND THAT QUOTES v3551. *** The stable-axis check
//   read measureGrowth's slope and r2 and asserted "no exponential trend". Both came back EXACTLY 0.00e+0 --
//   not a flat fit but the `xs.length < 8` GUARD, because a bounded perturbation NEVER RISES PAST THE FIT
//   BAND'S FLOOR and no points are ever collected. A CHECK WHOSE ANSWER WAS STRUCTURALLY GUARANTEED. Replaced
//   with an observable that belongs to the stable case: peak excursion as a multiple of the seed -- 1.000 and
//   1.000 for the outer axes against 1.10e8 for the intermediate one -- and measureGrowth now reports `points`
//   so a zero-sample fit can never again be mistaken for a flat one. THE GUARD WAS ALWAYS THERE; WHAT WAS
//   MISSING WAS ANY WAY TO TELL IT HAD FIRED.
//
// E -- THE SECOND ROUTE GRADES THE HALF THE FIRST NEVER TOUCHES. The world-frame angular momentum VECTOR is
//   constant, and reaching it needs the integrated quaternion, so it grades the ATTITUDE integration -- which
//   the body-frame invariants never see. Its drift HALVES EXACTLY when dt halves (ratios 2.000 / 2.000 /
//   2.000), so *** THE ATTITUDE INTEGRATOR IS FIRST ORDER WHILE w IS RK4: THE TWO HALVES OF THIS SOLVER ARE
