// v3905 -- THE COUPLER BETWEEN TWO SOLVERS GETS A GATE, AND THE EXPONENT IT CARRIES HAS NEVER BEEN OBSERVABLE.
//
// coverageTriage named physics/fluidBox3d.js the ONE genuine CANDIDATE among its six ungated non-scene modules.
// It was right, and the reason is the reason coupling code is dangerous: box3d is graded, Flip3D is graded, and
// NEITHER OF THEM GRADES THE EXCHANGE. A bug in the hand-off leaves both engines individually correct and only
// the pair wrong, so there is no module whose own selfcheck would go red -- no module owns the error.
//
// The exchange is almost entirely dimensional. World positions into grid positions, grid forces into world
// velocity deltas, grid torque into world angular impulse -- every one carries a power of `scale`, and a wrong
// power does not crash or produce NaN. It produces a number of the right shape, wrong by a factor.
//
// *** THE FINDING: THE TORQUE PATH CARRIES scale^2 AND THE ONLY CONSUMER RUNS AT scale 1. *** fluid-box3d.html
// builds the coupler with `scale: 1`, and it is the module's only consumer in this tree. At unit scale, scale^2
// and scale^1 ARE BIT-IDENTICAL DOUBLES -- 0.22, 0.26, 0.34 either way. So the one place the exponent could ever
// have been read is the one place it cannot be, and every frame this coupler has ever run has been blind to it.
// This is not a latent bug in dead code: the module's header names a non-unit host (ES ships) as the whole reason
// the parameter exists. At scale 5 the two spellings differ by exactly 5x.
//
// EIGHTEEN CHECKS ACROSS NINE SECTIONS: the guard refusing a half-implemented handle; externalBodies handed over
// so the bodies are not integrated twice; the Archimedes mass, density * 8 * grid-half-volume, exact at three
// scales; the world->grid mapping through (p - origin)/scale; the linear law dv = forceScale * scale * dt * F/m,
// exact at three scales and ADDED rather than assigned; the scale^2 torque sweep; the ORDER of the exchange,
// which no final value can reveal; the optional angular path degrading rather than throwing; and the real Flip3D
// end to end -- a density 0.25 box RISES from y=8 to 10.52 against -18 gravity while a density 4.0 box falls to
// -4.45, 14.96 apart.
//
// *** AND EVERY CHECK WAS VERIFIED BY PLANTING THE ERROR IT CLAIMS TO CATCH, BECAUSE A GATE THAT HAS ONLY EVER
// SEEN CORRECT CODE IS AN UNTESTED GATE. *** Five plants, one at a time, restored each time:
//   A torque scale^2 -> scale^1 (1 FAIL)   B nudge assigns instead of adds (2)   C externalBodies left false (1)
//   D mass drops the 8 (2)                 E world->grid multiplies (1)
//
// PLANT A IS THE RESULT THAT MATTERS AND I WOULD HAVE GUESSED IT WRONG. It is caught by EXACTLY ONE check out of
// eighteen -- not the linear law, not the real fluid, not the ordering. Everything else passes with the exponent
// wrong, because everything else either runs at unit scale or never touches torque. THE SCALE SWEEP IS THEREFORE
// LOAD-BEARING IN THE STRICT SENSE: weaken it to a single scale and the exponent stops being observable anywhere
// in this tree. Plants B and D were each caught TWICE, once by arithmetic and once by the real solver, and D's
// real-solver answer was qualitatively INVERTED -- a density 4.0 box rose to 14.80, because an 8x-light body is
// buoyant at any density. A HEAVY BOX THAT FLOATS IS THE KIND OF WRONG THAT SURVIVES REVIEW.
//
// coverageTriage: 342 -> 343 of 348 honest coverage, and its CANDIDATE line is now EMPTY -- the five that remain
// are 3 GLUE, 1 HARDWARE, 1 DEPENDENCY, all deliberately ungated. curriculum's frontier is UNCHANGED at six
// (3 GRADE, 3 DOOR) and two measured refusals: fluidBox3d was coverageTriage's finding, not curriculum's, and
// saying otherwise would claim a frontier this round did not touch.
