// its own header that the Dock merely provides the minitab and drawer, so the panel TRAVELS and only its host
// changes. All six tabs -- Publish, Account, Repos, Releases, Issues, Code -- arrive for free and cannot drift,
// because there is nothing to drift from. A SECOND GITHUB PANEL WRITTEN FOR THIS PAGE WOULD BE THE SECOND COPY
// THAT NEVER GETS UPDATED. The drawer reuses swekOverlay() for the same reason.
//
// *** AND MY FIRST WIRING WAS INERT, WHICH ONLY A REAL BROWSER SAID. *** I assumed a top-level `function` in a
// classic <script> is global. swekOverlay is inside an IIFE, so it is function-scoped, and a MODULE cannot see
// it: `typeof swekOverlay === "function"` came back FALSE, the button opened nothing, and it logged a warning
// nobody would ever read. THAT IS THE v3227 FAILURE VERBATIM -- a page that looks perfectly wired while one
// module is inert, with a single console line as the only evidence. Fixed by EXPOSING the one implementation,
// never by writing a second for the new caller.
//
// DRIVEN, NOT INFERRED: server.html served and loaded in Chromium, GitHub tab clicked, button clicked. The
// overlay opens, #ghPanelRoot is inside it, six tabs render, and the release button reads back verbatim. The
// only console errors are four bridge routes 404ing under a bare static server with no bridge -- each URL
