//
// AND THE FIRST FIX WAS NOT ENOUGH, WHICH ONLY THE BROWSER SAID. I added the missing "does this drawer already
// link to this page" guard, re-ran, AND THE TWELVE WERE STILL THERE. The reason is ORDER: placements resolves its
// fetch BEFORE the module moves the anchors in, so at the moment it checks the drawer is genuinely empty and
// appending is correct from what it can see. TWO ORDERINGS NEED TWO DEFENCES -- the guard for "mover first", and
// a pass after the mover for "placements first". Only the second one removes anything, only ever a
// [data-place-page] anchor, and only when the drawer already owns that href: the mover's anchors carry the icon
// and the title and are authoritative. placements keeps its adds-and-never-removes property, because declining a
// duplicate of a link already present is the same decision its own guard makes when the ordering lets it.
