// THE BOXING, MEASURED RATHER THAN EYEBALLED: 113 links across the drawers, 90 boxed and 23 NOT -- because the
// box was an INLINE STYLE applied by hand to each anchor in the Arriving markup, and 23 were simply missed. The
// two properties are independent: lab-export HAD its icon and no box. It is a CSS rule now, and THAT CHOICE IS
// THE POINT -- placements appends asynchronously, so a load-time JS styling pass would lose the race with links
// that have not arrived yet, while a rule applies the moment a node lands, whoever adds it. Links with no icon of
// their own get a neutral mark from an attribute, since CSS cannot ask whether text begins with an emoji and
// putting the glyph in the DOM would make it part of the link's own text.
