// v3914 -- THE EXACT-ZERO LEDGER HAD BEEN UNENFORCED FOR AS LONG AS census COULD NOT FINISH.
//
// v3913 gave census-selfcheck a budget and its hidden red became visible. I reported it as "vibrations.* and
// xpbd.weave", which is what fitted on the truncated line. *** THE REAL LIST IS THIRTY-TWO OBSERVABLES ACROSS
// SIXTEEN DEVICES *** -- fft, freerotation, clocks, geostats, fdtd, probe, seismic, nuclear, beam, centrifuge,
// galaxy, mpmstress, hands, kerrladder and the two I named. Reading a truncated line and reporting it as the
// whole list is its own small version of the mistake this tree keeps finding, and correcting it is the round.
//
// A gate that cannot finish cannot enforce its ledger, so the fresh list grew while nobody could see it. This
// round examines THE TWO CLUSTERS -- vibrations 6 and fft 6 -- and moves them to EXACT_OK, which is the register
// whose whole meaning is SOMEBODY LOOKED. The other twenty are named below and are NOT touched: adding a
// sentence to that register without doing the examination is precisely how it stops meaning anything.
//
// *** BOTH CLUSTERS HAVE A CONTROL, AND THE CONTROL IS THE POINT. ***
//
// VIBRATIONS: sumW2ErrRel and sumW4ErrRel compare moments of the eigenvalues lambda = w^2 -- sum(lambda) and
// sum(lambda^2), taken over the module's own frequencies -- against closed forms 2N(k/m) and (6N-2)(k/m)^2. The
// naming is offset by one BY DESIGN ("first moment" is the moment of lambda, so it lands on sumW2), and key4
// being computed by a function named secondMomentKey reads exactly like a copy-paste bug. I MEASURED BEFORE
// CONCLUDING: at N=12 the two sums are 24 and 70, small integers, exactly representable, and the summation
// reaches them to the bit. THE CONTROL IS ring AT N=32, where sum(lambda^2) comes out 189.99999999999997
// against 190 -- a residual of -2.84e-14 -- WHICH IS WHY ring.sumW4ErrRel IS NOT ON THE LIST. The same
// expression goes non-zero the moment the arithmetic stops being exact.
//
// FFT: a constant c gives |X[0]| = c*N and a sinusoid c*sin gives |X[k]| = c*N/2, both exactly, and nothing in
// fft.js is told either number. fftBind-selfcheck already asserts === 0 and says "NOT TOLERANCED -- EXACTLY
// ZERO" in the same line. THE CONTROL IS THE halfscale PLANT: the same two observables read 0.875 there. A
// check that could only ever return zero would read zero in that mode too.
//
// WHAT WAS NOT DONE, NAMED SO IT IS NOT MISTAKEN FOR DONE: freerotation 3, clocks 2, geostats 2, fdtd 2,
// probe 2, and one each from xpbd, seismic, nuclear, beam, centrifuge, galaxy, mpmstress, hands, kerrladder.
// Twenty observables, each needing its own measurement. EXACT_ZERO_BACKLOG IS FROZEN AND NOTHING WAS ADDED TO
// IT -- census says in as many words that adding to it is how a ratchet grows back.
//
// AND ONE THING I CHECKED RATHER THAN ASSUMED: vibrationsBind.mjs is v3336, five hundred versions older than my
// sixNplus6 plant. THESE ZEROS ARE NOT MINE. sixNplus6.sumW2ErrRel is on the list because the plant replaces the
// FOURTH moment's key only, leaving the second-moment comparison bit-identical to the honest arm -- it is the
// plant's blind partner, which is a property worth having and not a defect.
