// ruleExists alone, which is fine for something shown once; a banner on every load reading only that field
// would nag forever on a box whose firewall is switched OFF and whose port is already reachable. And the UAC
// prompt opens on the HOST's screen -- the tunnel dials out, so a remote really can be looking at this page
// over a port the LAN firewall is still blocking -- so a remote viewer is told the fact and not handed a
// button that would pop a dialog on a monitor nobody is sitting at.
