// The final check failed 11 against a cap of 8. Measured rather than argued, every one of ten moves real
// observables the moment it is perturbed past its own scale: blackhole:onsetTol at 2e-5, blackhole:escSteps at
// 600000, xpbd:tearStrain at 0.00106, acoustics:N at 200, freerotation:steps at 30000, refscan:maxDepth at 1,
// sdfmarch:epsilon at 1e-10, sdfmarch:maxSteps at 1, galaxy:zeroTol at 1, galaxy:maxHops at 2. THEY ARE ALL ONE
// KIND OF KNOB -- tolerances, caps and thresholds, whose entire job is to do NOTHING until crossed. perturb()
// moves a knob 1.1x, which asks for the LOCAL DERIVATIVE, and for this whole family that derivative is ZERO BY
// DESIGN: a slack cap does not begin to bind because it rose ten percent. The scan was not measuring them badly,
// it was measuring the wrong thing about them. FOURTH limitation of identical shape -- numeric-only comparison
// missed an array, one-at-a-time missed a gated knob, a multiplicative step missed an integer, and a small step
// misses everything whose response is a cliff rather than a slope. *** THE LADDER IS SAFE BY CONSTRUCTION, WHICH
// IS NOT A DETAIL. *** Integers escalate strictly DOWN: a slack cap only binds when lowered, and lowering a step
// count strictly REDUCES work, so escalation can never turn a 200000-step run into a 200-million-step one.
// Floats go three orders each way. *** AND ONE RUNG WAS ADDED AFTER A MEASUREMENT, RECORDED RATHER THAN SMOOTHED
// OVER. *** galaxy:zeroTol survived the +/-3-order ladder; its default is 1e-8 and the answer turns at the
// FIEDLER VALUE 0.0564, 5.6 MILLION times the default. The rung added is not "whatever makes galaxy pass": a
// dimensionless tolerance below one is meaningful over (0, 1], so a probe that never reaches O(1) has not spanned
// the knob at all. Stated as a property of that kind of knob, found by measuring where this one actually turns.
// *** THE ONE GENUINELY DEAD KNOB EXPOSED A DEVICE BUG. *** xpbd:h drives kernelIntegral, which reads
// 1.0000000000000153 at h = 0.25, 1.0 and 4.0 alike -- A NORMALISED KERNEL INTEGRATES TO UNITY AT EVERY SUPPORT
// RADIUS, so invariance IS the graded property and dead is correct and permanent. But the same return object
// carried restDensity from latticeRestDensity() CALLED WITH NO ARGUMENTS, pinned at that function's own h = 0.25
// while kernelIntegral tracked the caller's h: two numbers in one object at two different smoothing lengths with
// nothing saying so, and it is not a small difference (232.4 at h = 0.2 against 75.9 at h = 1.0). REMOVED rather
// than wired to c.h, because the two h's are not the same quantity -- c.h is the kernel support radius this mode
// integrates over, latticeRestDensity's is the smoothing length of a lattice at spacing 0.16, and at c.h = 1.0
// every particle in the 6^3 lattice is a neighbour so "rest density of a packing" degenerates into an all-pairs
// sum. Passing it through would have made the number MOVE while making it MEAN LESS. Second advertised-and-unread
// key this gate has caught, after nuclear:A/Z. *** AND THE BARE COUNT IS GONE. *** Three checks in this file and
